# Dev Notes 50 — Runtime Capability Execute-Action Orchestration v1

**Date:** 2026-06-18  
**Branch:** `runtime-capability-execute-action-orchestration-v1`  
**Status:** Merged to `main` and main-inspected for the declared contract/composition-only scope; assistant sandbox syntax checks, targeted execute-action orchestration smoke, existing contract-chain smokes, fixture helper check, worker import-cycle check, public-entrypoint guard, artifact/package guard, package extraction/recheck, Michael local Windows/MINGW64 candidate checks, direct GitHub branch inspection, and direct GitHub `main` inspection passed. No real-runtime test is required for the declared scope because this branch does not touch runtime/worker/lifecycle/native execution surfaces.

---

## 1. Purpose

This branch adds a narrow, modular, contract-only composition seam after `runtime-backend-adapter-execution-interface-v1`.

The branch proves that the accepted execute-action descriptor chain can be composed into one execute-action orchestration descriptor without starting execution.

Current descriptor chain:

```text
actionEnvelope
  -> capability bus action
  -> router route plan
  -> service plan
  -> backend adapter plan
  -> capability execution plan
  -> executor skeleton handoff descriptor
  -> backend adapter invocation descriptor
```

New branch output:

```text
accepted execute-action plan
  -> executor skeleton handoff descriptor
  -> backend adapter invocation descriptor
  -> execute-action orchestration descriptor
```

The new descriptor is a bus-owned composition artifact. It does not execute actions, call services, call backend adapters, call `workerBridge`, import `llama_worker`, enqueue requests, stream tokens, load models, or touch lifecycle behavior.

---

## 2. Modular ownership

Ownership boundaries preserved:

```text
runtime/bus/executeAction/ owns execute-action composition/orchestration contracts.
runtime/execution/ owns capability execution and executor skeleton descriptors.
runtime/backends/ owns backend adapter and backend invocation descriptors.
runtime/router/ owns route validation and route/model/profile compatibility.
runtime/models/ owns model bundle metadata.
runtime/profiles/ owns hardware profile metadata.
runtime.mjs / workerBridge / llama_worker own real runtime/native behavior and remain untouched.
```

The orchestration helper consumes existing execution/backend validation helpers instead of duplicating backend or executor internals.

