## 4. New contract identity

```text
contractVersion: capability-bus-execute-action-orchestration.v1
status: accepted
```

Boundary metadata:

```js
{
    orchestration: "composition-only",
    executable: false,
    adapterInvocation: "contract-only",
    runtimeWiring: "not-wired",
    nativeExecution: "not-wired"
}
```

Ordered chain metadata:

```text
actionEnvelope
capabilityBusAction
capabilityRoutePlan
capabilityServicePlan
backendAdapterPlan
capabilityExecutionPlan
capabilityExecutorSkeletonPlan
backendAdapterInvocationDescriptor
```

---

## 5. Contract behavior

New helpers:

```js
validateCapabilityBusExecuteActionOrchestrationDescriptor(value)
normalizeCapabilityBusExecuteActionOrchestrationDescriptor(value)
assertCapabilityBusExecuteActionOrchestrationDescriptor(value)
```

Behavior:

```text
accepts a current accepted execute-action plan
accepts an already normalized execute-action orchestration descriptor
normalizes accepted execute-action plans into orchestration descriptors
derives executor skeleton handoff descriptors through the existing execution helper
derives backend adapter invocation descriptors through the existing backend helper
embeds copy-isolated child descriptors for contract visibility
requires non-executable / not-wired / contract-only boundary metadata
rejects raw backend adapter plans as direct orchestration inputs
rejects raw capability execution plans as direct orchestration inputs
rejects unknown top-level, orchestration, action, and boundary fields
rejects forbidden runtime/worker/native/model-path/backend-execution keys in orchestration-owned metadata
```

The branch intentionally keeps accepted execute-action plans as the only non-normalized top-level source. Lower-level descriptors remain owned by their own namespaces and cannot be used as direct orchestration inputs.

